    "processingDescription": "Private complete schema-2 virtual-robot fixture. This supersedes the rejected V14 candidate: its 0.015 kg body was paired with 1.2 m-chord wings, yielding D24 fixed-body loads up to 5.52 N and 3.25 N m and an invalid free release. V15 restored a compact 0.56 m total span, 0.14-to-0.09 m tapered wing, 0.015 kg total-mass ledger, 0.002 kg per-wing rigid-plate properties, and body inertias sized for that packaged robot, but its D12 five-cycle pitch-offset map produced no lift capable of supporting the mass ledger (best 0.000177 N versus 0.147100 N weight). V16 raised the same robot to 8 Hz and 0.80 rad; it passed the static Mach estimate but became non-finite before its 512-step D12 moving-boundary gate and is rejected. V17 was the intermediate 5 Hz, 0.55 rad waveform; it produced 0.7608 N mean force over a 512-step D12 transient, but became non-finite before 1,600 steps at both D12 and D16 and is rejected. V18 preserved the V17 physical robot but halved lattice reference speed from 0.04 to 0.02, reducing only D3Q19 lattice velocity and timestep. Its 4,000-step D12 moving-boundary run still became non-finite, so the high-authority rigid-wing coupling is rejected rather than attributed to Mach or timestep alone. A future wing-structure/coupling change must demonstrate a stable five-cycle fixed-body force window before coupled release, refinement, momentum closure, or Numi policy promotion. This is not a measured Deetjen or biological specimen."
  },
